From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:34:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/fbdev-shmem: flush the kernel mapping before reporting
 damage

fbcon and the fbdev drawing helpers write the framebuffer through its
vmap of the shmem pages, and the device then reads those pages when the
damaged lines are transferred. An architecture whose kernel aliases are
not always coherent with the pages behind them, such as the UML Darwin
port with 4 KiB pages, must publish the lines first, so the fbdev dirty
callback brackets the clip with flush_kernel_vmap_range(), as drivers
that share a vmap with a device already do. It costs nothing where the
architecture has no such hook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fbdev_shmem.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fbdev_shmem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fbdev_shmem.c
index d435caed70029f0eb55908bb7c22d99c9750f95a..48abddfd7a001c643c809d8fe97af0b30fa545af 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fbdev_shmem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fbdev_shmem.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/export.h>
 #include <linux/fb.h>
+#include <linux/highmem.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fbdev_shmem.h>
@@ -108,12 +109,21 @@ static int drm_fbdev_shmem_helper_fb_dirty(struct drm_fb_helper *helper,
 					   struct drm_clip_rect *clip)
 {
 	struct drm_device *dev = helper->dev;
+	unsigned int pitch = helper->fb->pitches[0];
 	int ret;
 
 	/* Call damage handlers only if necessary */
 	if (!(clip->x1 < clip->x2 && clip->y1 < clip->y2))
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * The fbdev drawing helpers write the vmapped buffer while the device
+	 * reads the pages behind it. Where a kernel alias is not coherent with
+	 * those pages, the damaged lines must reach them first.
+	 */
+	flush_kernel_vmap_range(helper->info->screen_buffer + clip->y1 * pitch,
+				(clip->y2 - clip->y1) * pitch);
+
 	if (helper->fb->funcs->dirty) {
 		ret = helper->fb->funcs->dirty(helper->fb, NULL, 0, 0, clip, 1);
 		if (drm_WARN_ONCE(dev, ret, "Dirty helper failed: ret=%d\n", ret))
